## Interface: 120100
## Title: |cff11ace9Buzzard Frames|r Options
## Notes: The new options panel for Buzzard Frames. Loads on demand, the first time options are opened.
## Author: Serina
## Version: 1.0
## X-Category: UI
# The same icon Buzzard Frames wears in the AddOn list, so the pair reads
# as one addon. The path crosses into the BuzzardFrames folder, which is
# safe: this addon hard-depends on it, so the file is always there.
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\BuzzardFrames\Media\buzzardRes

# Loaded ON DEMAND, by BuzzardFrames, the first time the panel is opened.
#
# The library and the panel are a meaningful amount of code to parse,
# and a reader who never opens the options never pays for it. Nothing
# here runs at login.
## LoadOnDemand: 1

# BuzzardFrames must be present and loaded FIRST: everything here reads its
# saved variables and calls its API, and this addon owns no SavedVariables
# of its own -- geometry included, which lives in BuzzardFrames' db.global.
## Dependencies: BuzzardFrames

# The panel library, vendored into Libs as an embedded library. It brings
# no LibStub of its own -- BuzzardFrames' is the only copy, and it is
# already loaded by the time this addon does -- and no .toc; the order
# below comes from the library's own .toc. Regenerate with
# Tools\vendor_buzzardpanel.py rather than editing the copy.
Libs\BuzzardPanel\BuzzardPanel.xml

# The panel itself, then its pages. Panel.lua publishes the addon table
# and must come first: every page file hangs its builder off it.
#
# The pages after it are in ROUTE order rather than the order they were
# written, so this list reads as the tree does. Order is not otherwise
# load-bearing between them: each one only adds a method to the table
# Panel.lua published, and nothing is called until the panel is opened.
Panel.lua
Pages_Testing.lua

# The border style control, shared by every page that draws one: the six
# of them stored the same four values and offered the same list, with the
# rounded frame's WEIGHT sitting in it as if it were a shape. Defines no
# page of its own.
Pages_BorderStyle.lua

# Raid / Party Frames
Pages_RaidPartyGeneral.lua
Pages_Frames.lua
Pages_Sorting.lua

# The aura pages. Pages_AuraShared.lua holds the storage routing, the
# scoped refresh and the per-subtab per-Layout strip that all three of
# them use; it defines no page of its own. Load order between them does
# not matter -- each only adds a method to the table Panel.lua published,
# and nothing runs until the panel is opened -- but the shared file is
# listed first because that is the order it reads in.
Pages_AuraShared.lua
Pages_Buffs.lua
Pages_Debuffs.lua
# The Buff List entry's four visual subtabs (Icon, Icon Effects, Cooldown
# Text, Frame Effects), which Pages_AuraContainers.lua asks for when it
# builds an entry's page.
Pages_SingleBuffVisuals.lua
Pages_AuraContainers.lua

Pages_AuraText.lua
Pages_Text.lua
Pages_HealthPower.lua
Pages_Borders.lua
Pages_Absorbs.lua
Pages_Icons.lua
Pages_CastBar.lua
Pages_Tooltips.lua
Pages_Layouts.lua
Pages_Preview.lua

# Custom Frame Groups. LAST of the Raid/Party group on purpose: these two
# render the page builders above against a custom frame group's own flat,
# so they read after the files they route. Nothing here is CALLED at load
# -- the section files resolve every builder by name, at the moment a route
# is opened -- but the order is the order a reader should meet them in.
#
# Pages_CustomFrameSections.lua first: it defines BuzzardFramesOptions:BF(),
# the accessor every page file above now goes through, and the assembler
# Pages_CustomFrames.lua's own pages are put together by.
Pages_CustomFrameSections.lua
Pages_CustomFrames.lua

# Unit Frames. Pages_UnitFramesShared.lua first: it holds the write-through
# root, the relayout helpers and the four subtabs both the player and the
# target carry, and the two files after it hang their pages off it.
# Pages_UnitFramesGeneral.lua publishes UnitFramesOff, which Panel.lua's
# route builder asks before it declares this section's children -- but that
# is a runtime call, so the order here is for the reader.
Pages_UnitFramesShared.lua
Pages_UnitFramesGeneral.lua
Pages_UnitFramesPlayer.lua
Pages_UnitFramesTarget.lua
Pages_UnitFramesOther.lua
Pages_UFLayouts.lua

# Incoming Casts
Pages_IncomingCasts.lua

# Profiles. Pages_ProfilesShared.lua first: it carries the import pipeline
# (the legacy decoders, the decode/import state, the copy window) that the
# Import and Export tabs run, and defines no page of its own.
Pages_ProfilesShared.lua
Pages_Profiles.lua

# Global Styles. Pages_GlobalStylesShared.lua first: it carries the write
# fan-out every Global Styles field pushes through (one write lands on the
# Raid/Party global section, every Layout, every custom frame group and the
# unit frames) and the "Apply Changes To" card, and defines no page of its
# own. The page files after it are in the section's own tree order.
Pages_GlobalStylesShared.lua
Pages_Colors.lua
Pages_GlobalStylesHealth.lua
Pages_GlobalStylesBorders.lua
Pages_GlobalStylesAbsorbs.lua
Pages_GlobalStylesIcons.lua
Pages_GlobalStylesText.lua
Pages_GlobalStylesAuras.lua
